WEBVTT

00:08:59.577 --> 00:09:01.120
to regain agency

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:03.789
and feel like they haven't
taken everything from us.

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:06.333
And as Maya Angelou says,

00:09:06.333 --> 00:09:08.043
there’s nothing more agonizing

00:09:08.043 --> 00:09:10.629
than an untold story
hanging inside of you --

00:09:10.629 --> 00:09:12.214
not directly quoting.

00:09:12.798 --> 00:09:16.468
And I think we really needed
to regain a sense of order,

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:17.970
find our coordinate,

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:19.138
a sense of home.

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:21.056
And like after World War I,

00:09:21.056 --> 00:09:24.476
a lot of European artists
went back into classicism,

00:09:24.476 --> 00:09:28.147
trying to run away
from this feeling of destruction

00:09:28.147 --> 00:09:29.440
that the war had brought in

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:33.360
and stepped away from
the experimentalism that came before,